  "question": {
    "text": "The derivative of $e^{x^3}$ with respect to $\\log x$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "X43Na",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{e}^{\\mathrm{x}^3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "itkgq",
      "text": "$3 \\mathrm{x}^2 2 \\mathrm{e}^{\\mathrm{x}^3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PCpLM",
      "text": "$3 \\mathrm{x}^3 \\mathrm{e}^{\\mathrm{x}^3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ZCpE1",
      "text": "$3 \\mathrm{x}^3 \\mathrm{e}^{\\mathrm{x}^3}+3 \\mathrm{x}^2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $y=\\mathrm{e}^{\\mathrm{x}^3}, \\mathrm{z}=\\log \\mathrm{x}$<br />On differentiating w.r.t.x, we get<br />$\\frac{d y}{d x}=e^{x^3}\\left(3 x^2\\right)=3 x^2 e^{x^3} \\text { and } \\frac{d z}{d x}=\\frac{1}{x}$<br />$\\therefore \\frac{d y}{d z}=\\frac{\\frac{d y}{d x}}{\\frac{d z}{d x}}=\\frac{3 x^2 e^{x^3}}{\\left(\\frac{1}{x}\\right)}=3 x^3 e^{x^3}$",
    "image": null
  },
